<h2 ultimate-bold-correct=3D""> ESP32 / WROOM </h2>


<img src=3D"https://micropython.org/resources/micropython-media/boards/ESP3=
2_GENERIC/esp32_devkitc.jpg" class=3D"img-responsive thumb hero">


<div>
<strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Vendor:</strong> Espressif
</div>


<div>
<strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Features:</strong> BLE, External Flash, =
WiFi
</div>


<div>
    <strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Source on GitHub:</strong> <a href=
=3D"https://github.com/micropython/micropython/tree/master/ports/esp32/boar=
ds/ESP32_GENERIC">esp32/ESP32_GENERIC</a>
</div>


<div>
<strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">More info:</strong> <a href=3D"https://w=
ww.espressif.com/en/products/modules">Website</a>
</div>


<p>The following files are firmware that should work on most ESP32-based bo=
ards
with 4MiB or more of flash, including WROOM WROVER, SOLO, PICO, and MINI mo=
dules.</p>
<p>This board has multiple variants available:</p>
<ul>
<li>If your board is based on a WROVER module, or otherwise has SPIRAM (als=
o known
as PSRAM) then it's recommended to use the "spiram" variant. Look for headi=
ng
<strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Support for SPIRAM / WROVER)</strong>.</=
li>
<li>If your board has a ESP32-D2WD chip (with only 2MiB flash) then use the=
 "d2wd"
variant. Look for heading <strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">ESP32 D2WD</st=
rong>.</li>
<li>If your board has a single-core ESP32 (e.g. the "SOLO" modules) then ch=
oose
the "unicore" variant. Look for heading <strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">=
ESP32 Unicore</strong>.</li>
<li>If you'd like to perform Over-the-Air updates of the MicroPython firmwa=
re,
then choose the "ota" variant. This variant has less room in the flash for
Python files as a result of supporting OTA. Look for heading <strong ultima=
te-bold-correct=3D"">Support for
OTA</strong>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Otherwise, download the generic variant (under the first heading below).=
</p>
<h2 ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Installation instructions</h2>
<p>Program your board using the esptool.py program, found <a href=3D"https:=
//docs.espressif.com/projects/esptool/en/latest/esp32/">here</a>.</p>
<p><em ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Windows users:</em> You may find the inst=
alled program is called <code>esptool</code> instead of <code>esptool.py</c=
ode>.</p>
<h3>Erasing</h3>
<p>If you are putting MicroPython on your board for the first time then you=
 should
first erase the entire flash using:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-bash">esptool.py erase_flash
</code></pre>
<p><code>esptool.py</code> will try to detect the serial port with the ESP3=
2 automatically,
but if this fails or there might be more than one Espressif-based device
attached to your computer then pass the <code>--port</code> option with the=
 name of the
target serial port. For example:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-bash">esptool.py --port PORTNAME erase_flash
</code></pre>
<ul>
<li>On Linux, the port name is usually similar to <code>/dev/ttyUSB</code> =
or <code>/dev/ttyACM0</code>.</li>
<li>On Mac, the port name is usually similar to <code>/dev/cu.usbmodem01</c=
ode>.</li>
<li>On Windows, the port name is usually similar to <code>COM4</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Flashing</h3>
<p>Then deploy the firmware to the board, starting at address 0x1000:</p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-bash">esptool.py --baud 460800 write_flash 0x1=
000 ESP32_BOARD_NAME-DATE-VERSION.bin
</code></pre>
<p>Replace <code>ESP32_BOARD_NAME-DATE-VERSION.bin</code> with the <code>.b=
in</code> file downloaded from this page.</p>
<p>As above, if <code>esptool.py</code> can't automatically detect the seri=
al port
then you can pass it explicitly on the command line instead. For example:</=
p>
<pre><code class=3D"language-bash">esptool.py --port PORTNAME --baud 460800=
 write_flash 0x1000 ESP32_BOARD_NAME-DATE-VERSION.bin
</code></pre>
<h3>Troubleshooting</h3>
<p>If flashing starts and then fails partway through, try removing the <cod=
e>--baud 460800</code> option to flash at the slower default speed.</p>
<p>If these steps don't work, consult the <a href=3D"https://docs.micropyth=
on.org/en/latest/esp32/tutorial/intro.html#troubleshooting-installation-pro=
blems">MicroPython ESP32 Troubleshooting
steps</a>
and the <a href=3D"https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esptool/en/latest/es=
p32/esptool/basic-options.html">esptool
documentation</a>.</p>
<p><strong ultimate-bold-correct=3D"">Important</strong>: From the options =
below, download the <code>.bin</code> file for your board.</p>




